  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nRewards in `notifyRewardAmount` are transferred even when `IVoter(voter).totalWeight()` is zero. In that case `_ratio` remains `0`, so the global index never moves. The funds stay in `GaugeManager`, but no gauge can ever accrue them.\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol#L268-L288\n\n```solidity\nfunction notifyRewardAmount(uint256 amount) external {\n        require(msg.sender == minter, \"NA\");\n        IERC20Upgradeable(base).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n\n        uint256 _ratio = 0;\n        uint256 totalWeight = IVoter(voter).totalWeight();\n        if(totalWeight > 0) _ratio = amount * 1e18 / Math.max(totalWeight, 1);     // 1e18 adjustment is removed during claim\n        if (_ratio > 0) {\n            index += _ratio;\n        }\n\n        emit NotifyReward(msg.sender, base, amount);\n    }\n\n    function distributeFees() external nonReentrant {\n        uint256 i = 0;\n        uint256 poolsLength = pools.length;\n        for (i; i < poolsLength; i++) {\n            address _pool = pools[i];\n            _distributeFees(_pool);\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nWhen `_updateForAfterDistribution` runs and a pool’s live weight is zero, it only updates `supplyIndex` to the current index. There’s no attempt to refund those emissions to the minter or redistribute them. Any tokens associated with that index delta simply remain stranded in the manager.\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol#L373-L394\n\nThe codebase doesn’t contain a follow‑up mechanism that replays the stuck balance once weights return or that lets governance claw it back. Killed gauges do [refund](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol#L389), but the zero-weight path skips that logic.\n\n\nAs a result, minted emissions can get wedged inside `GaugeManager` indefinitely (e.g., first epoch before anyone votes, or a pool zeroes its weight before distribution). They never reach gauges, never return to the minter, and can’t be recovered without a manual rescue\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nRevert `notifyRewardAmount` when `totalWeight == 0`, or stage the amount in a pending bucket and apply it once weights go positive. Similarly, when `_supplied == 0` but `index > supplyIndex`, either refund the delta to the minter (mirroring the killed-gauge branch) or reallocate it across active pools.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {C4PoCTestbed} from \"./C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\nimport {ERC20} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\n\ncontract MockERC20 is ERC20 {\n    constructor(string memory name_, string memory symbol_) ERC20(name_, symbol_) {}\n\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        _mint(to, amount);\n    }\n}\n\n/**\n * @title C4PoC\n * @notice A complete deployment of the CL contract suite\n * @dev All available variables are showcased in the commented\n *      storage slots of the contract.\n */\n\n// Deployed contracts\n// ProxyAdmin public proxyAdmin;\n// PermissionsRegistry public permissionsRegistry;\n// VeArtProxyUpgradeable public veArtProxy;\n// TokenHandler public tokenHandler;\n\n// HYBR public hybr;\n// RewardHYBR public rewardHybr;\n// GrowthHYBR public gHybr;\n// VotingEscrow public votingEscrow;\n\n// GaugeFactory public gaugeFactory;\n// GaugeFactoryCL public gaugeFactoryCL;\n\n// PairFactory public thenaFiFactory;\n\n// GaugeManager public gaugeManager;\n// BribeFactoryV3 public bribeFactoryV3;\n\n// MinterUpgradeable public minter;\n// RewardsDistributor public rewardsDistributor;\n\n// VoterV3 public voter;\n\n// address public deployer;\n\n// Imported contracts\n// address public clPoolFactory;\n// address public clPoolImplementation;\n// address public clNonfungiblePositionManager;\n// address public clNftPositionDescriptor;\n// address public clSwapRouter;\n// address public clQuoter;\n// address public clSwapFeeModule;\n// address public clUnstakedFeeModule;\n// address public clProtocolFeeModule;\n\n// Administrative Addresses\n// address public team = 0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266;\n// address public poolFactoryOwner = 0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266;\n// address public feeManager = 0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266;\n\ncontract C4PoC is C4PoCTestbed {\n    uint256 internal constant MAX_LOCK_DURATION = 2 * 365 days;\n    uint256 internal constant NO_VOTING_WINDOW = 300;\n\n    MockERC20 internal tokenA;\n    MockERC20 internal tokenB;\n    MockERC20 internal tokenC;\n\n    address internal poolAB;\n    address internal poolAC;\n\n    address internal gaugeAB;\n    address internal gaugeAC;\n\n    uint256 internal tokenId;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        bribeFactoryV3.initialize(\n            address(voter),\n            address(gaugeManager),\n            address(permissionsRegistry),\n            address(tokenHandler)\n        );\n\n        permissionsRegistry.setRoleFor(address(this), \"GOVERNANCE\");\n        permissionsRegistry.setRoleFor(address(this), \"GENESIS_MANAGER\");\n\n        tokenA = new MockERC20(\"Token A\", \"TKNA\");\n        tokenB = new MockERC20(\"Token B\", \"TKNB\");\n        tokenC = new MockERC20(\"Token C\", \"TKNC\");\n\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](3);\n        tokens[0] = address(tokenA);\n        tokens[1] = address(tokenB);\n        tokens[2] = address(tokenC);\n        tokenHandler.whitelistTokens(tokens);\n        tokenHandler.whitelistConnector(address(tokenA));\n\n        poolAB = thenaFiFactory.createPair(address(tokenA), address(tokenB), false);\n        poolAC = thenaFiFactory.createPair(address(tokenA), address(tokenC), false);\n\n        (gaugeAB,,) = gaugeManager.createGauge(poolAB, 0);\n        (gaugeAC,,) = gaugeManager.createGauge(poolAC, 0);\n\n        hybr.approve(address(votingEscrow), type(uint256).max);\n        tokenId = votingEscrow.create_lock(1_000e18, MAX_LOCK_DURATION);\n    }\n\n\n    function testUnvotedEmissionsRemainStuck() external {\n        uint256 week = minter.WEEK();\n\n        // Mint emissions with zero total weight\n        vm.warp(week + 10);\n        uint256 balanceBefore = hybr.balanceOf(address(gaugeManager));\n        assertEq(balanceBefore, 0, \"manager not empty before mint\");\n        minter.update_period();\n        uint256 stuckAmount = hybr.balanceOf(address(gaugeManager));\n        assertGt(stuckAmount, 0, \"emission not minted\");\n\n        // Cast votes after the first emission is already stuck\n        vm.warp(week + NO_VOTING_WINDOW + 20);\n        address[] memory poolsToVote = new address[](2);\n        poolsToVote[0] = poolAB;\n        poolsToVote[1] = poolAC;\n        uint256[] memory weights = new uint256[](2);\n        weights[0] = 50;\n        weights[1] = 50;\n        voter.vote(tokenId, poolsToVote, weights);\n\n        // Attempt to distribute; stuck balance should remain inside GaugeManager\n        address[] memory gaugesToDistribute = new address[](2);\n        gaugesToDistribute[0] = gaugeAB;\n        gaugesToDistribute[1] = gaugeAC;\n        gaugeManager.distribute(gaugesToDistribute);\n\n        assertEq(hybr.balanceOf(gaugeAB), 0, \"gauge A should not receive stuck emissions\");\n        assertEq(hybr.balanceOf(gaugeAC), 0, \"gauge C should not receive stuck emissions\");\n        assertEq(hybr.balanceOf(address(gaugeManager)), stuckAmount, \"stuck emissions remain in GaugeManager\");\n        assertEq(gaugeManager.claimable(gaugeAB), 0, \"claimable for gauge A remains zero\");\n        assertEq(gaugeManager.claimable(gaugeAC), 0, \"claimable for gauge C remains zero\");\n    }\n}\n\n```",
